WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.270
The explosive third season finale of You has
everything, from roast dinners to die for,

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:09.810
to extreme cage therapy, and a big twist setting
up Season 4.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.010
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:15.010
I'm Jan and in this video I'm breaking down
all the things you might have missed in the

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:20.230
ending of You Season 3, the clues that predicted
the shocking conclusion, and what the future

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:21.369
holds for Joe.

00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:25.160
We'll be talking spoilers, so take care if
you're not all caught up.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:29.240
The fact that Joe would end up permanently
severing his and his son's ties with Love

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.590
in the finale was foreshadowed all the way
back in the opening scene of the season where

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.510
he cut the umbilical cord between Love and
baby Henry.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:42.000
And, just an episode later, it was also hinted
at by the couple's therapist who had no idea

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.090
of the serial killers she had for clients.

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:45.870
Neither one of you is gonna kill your spouse.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.800
You're many things, but you are not murderers.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.350
The problems in Joe and Love's marriage come
to a head in the final episode when she serves

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.990
him roast chicken, which she figured out was
his favourite meal on their very first night

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.190
out together.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.190
Perfect bite?

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.190
Perfect.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:04.270
That was also the night Joe found out about
Love's dead husband and when they both discovered

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:06.000
how alike they were.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.280
Fast-forward to now where it's the dying days
of their relationship, and roast chicken and

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.790
dead husband discussion are back on the menu,
with Love admitting to killing her first spouse

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:19.350
by accident when she tried to temporarily
paralyse him with aconite to stop him from

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.749
leaving her.

00:01:20.749 --> 00:01:25.530
And now it's Joe's turn as he unwittingly
grabs a poison-laced carving knife that Love

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:26.560
set to trap him!

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.430
This time, I'm letting it absorb through the
skin.

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:30.840
None of this would be happening if you hadn't
grabbed a weapon.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:35.260
In their twisted obsession, Love and Joe are
almost mirror images of each other, so she

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.299
realised he'd go for the knife.

00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:39.530
Love knows me better than anyone ever has.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:42.600
I'm starting to understand why that's so terrifying.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.841
By the way, notice how Love used a glove to
handle the carving knife before this so she

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:50.479
wouldn't get the poison on her own hand.

00:01:50.479 --> 00:01:54.729
Love's choice of aconite, which is commonly
known as wolfsbane, has an extra level of

00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:59.389
meaning in this show because the word "wolf"
used to be part of her and Joe's special love

00:01:59.389 --> 00:02:00.389
language.

00:02:00.389 --> 00:02:01.389
I love you.

00:02:01.389 --> 00:02:02.389
Is there another word we can use?

00:02:02.389 --> 00:02:03.389
I wolf you.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.389
I wolf you too.

00:02:04.389 --> 00:02:09.069
And in Season 3, when Joe and Love are struggling
to enjoy sex together, he bemoans the fact

00:02:09.069 --> 00:02:11.189
they don't say "I wolf you" any more.

00:02:11.189 --> 00:02:12.709
We've been domesticated.

00:02:12.709 --> 00:02:13.940
I wolf you.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:14.940
Wolf?

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:15.940
Or dog-on-a-leash?

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.590
There were also a few possible hints in Season
2 towards Love's eventual use of wolfsbane

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:25.569
on Joe when she playfully attacked him with
a toy wolf, a gesture that also signalled

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:29.930
her penchant for slashing her victims' throats;
and, there was also the real wolf the Quinns

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:33.760
brought to the wellness weekend which snarled
aggressively at Joe.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:38.420
Interestingly, after Marienne's advice to
listen to the 'tiny voice' in her own head,

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.360
Love realises how many things are wrong in
her relationship.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.239
I mean, you gaslit me so hard.

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:45.239
I'm not the problem.

00:02:45.239 --> 00:02:46.239
My husband is the problem.

00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:50.781
And she decides to cut her losses and goes
to kill Joe with the same cut-throat MO she

00:02:50.781 --> 00:02:53.099
used on most of her previous victims.

00:02:53.099 --> 00:02:56.780
But Joe's already turned the tables on his
mirror-image wife;

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:00.860
she just doesn't realise she's been hoisted
by her own petard until he stabs her in the

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:03.750
leg with a syringe full of her own deadly
wolfsbane.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.250
Our love language is violence.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:11.010
And in a little visual gag, the jar of poison
Joe pulled the wolfsbane from was labelled

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.010
'Dye Sample'.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:16.920
Oh, and despite Joe's unfavourable views of
the Madre Linda dads when he first meets them..

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:21.129
the haze of narcissistic delusion that just
the right biohack, you'll live forever.

00:03:21.129 --> 00:03:24.700
..it's actually biohacking that saves his
life in the end.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:29.569
By the way, notice that Joe didn't eat anything
before he saw Love eat because he was already

00:03:29.569 --> 00:03:34.269
worried about being poisoned, a call-back
to when Love brought him muffins after trapping

00:03:34.269 --> 00:03:35.849
him in his cage in Season 2.

00:03:35.849 --> 00:03:37.010
Is this what you're afraid of?

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:38.010
No poison, Joe!

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:42.740
Given their one-upmanship with poisonous wolfsbane,
Love and Joe have certainly brought very literal

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:45.599
meaning to the term 'toxic relationship'.

00:03:45.599 --> 00:03:51.280
Joe's recipe for a successful getaway involves
cooking up a salacious story to keep everyone's

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:56.280
minds occupied with juicy details, the aim
being to stop them asking awkward questions

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.640
about how true it is.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:02.459
And he certainly knows his audience because
the people of Madre Linda love to gossip and

00:04:02.459 --> 00:04:06.379
are more interested in manufactured reality
than reality itself.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:09.499
For the public, the brand is conventional
monogamy.

00:04:09.499 --> 00:04:14.860
So, Joe sprinkles just enough believable information
into the tale he concocts.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:19.310
Cue him preparing a Chicken Pot Pie, using
against Love the fact that she's a "trained

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:22.310
pastry chef" and well-known as the town's
baker.

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:27.310
And it's all somewhat ironic that part of
Joe ends up in Love's chicken pie given chicken

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:32.090
was his perfect bite in their early loved-up
days and their wedding vows even included

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:35.090
pastry:
You said you would always share a bite of

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:37.220
your pastry with me, no matter what.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:41.080
Intriguingly, Joe's final plan was foreshadowed
in the opening episode:

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:46.080
This isn't some German fairytale where a witch
keeps me locked up till it's time to eat me.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:50.020
That's a shout-out to Hansel and Gretel where
the witch who plans to eat the children is

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:53.950
outwitted by them and ends up dying in her
own fiery oven.

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:58.600
On top of that, the way Joe turns Love into
a legendary figure akin to the baker who made

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:03.009
murder victims into meat pies in Sweeney Todd..
the Mrs Lovett of Madre Linda

00:05:03.009 --> 00:05:07.750
..is especially apt because in the musical
version of that story, Todd burns the baker

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:12.640
Mrs Lovett to death after shoving her into
an oven, while in the original story he kills

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:13.860
her with poison.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:18.530
And let's not forget the little box of gruesome
mementos that Joe leaves at Love's side.

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:22.870
As well as Gil's driver's license, there's
a bunch of teeth, probably Natalie's.

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:28.669
We know Joe removed them to avoid dental records,
as he did with Benji, and remember he wouldn't

00:05:28.669 --> 00:05:30.440
tell Love what he'd done with them.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:33.250
I just don't wanna find them in a hidey-hole
in my house.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.250
You won't.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.250
It's safer if you don't know.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:39.300
Given that earlier in the same episode, Love
refused to tell Joe what she'd done with Candace

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.830
and Delilah's bodies...

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:44.919
It's safer if you don't know
..I imagine Joe kept the teeth in case Love

00:05:44.919 --> 00:05:47.880
tried pinning those Season 2 deaths on him.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:52.750
After all, he admits to hanging on to another
of Natalie's possessions for similar reasons

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:56.509
and suggests using that to frame Matthew for
her murder.

00:05:56.509 --> 00:06:01.360
With all the evidence in place to frame his
dead wife, Joe sets the house on fire to ensure

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:05.759
the crime scene is damaged enough to make
the faked murder-suicide more plausible.

00:06:05.759 --> 00:06:11.190
He leaves the burning building to go in search
of Marienne, exactly as was foreshadowed several

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:12.560
episodes earlier.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.110
For you, Marienne, I will walk through fire.

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:19.110
There were also some other early hints that
telegraphed how Love would end up getting

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:21.120
the blame for torching the house.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:24.960
All you ever showed me was to get the prince,
build a castle, and then burn it all to the

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:26.150
f!$*%@# ground.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:30.669
Then there was Love's mother Dottie who set
light to her own vineyard during a bitter

00:06:30.669 --> 00:06:35.700
divorce, which would doubtless lead the town
gossips to say, "Like mother, like daughter".

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.910
And at the library gala when Joe was panicking
about Love and Marienne meeting up, his inner

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:42.800
monologue predicted the events of the final
episode.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:47.520
I should orchestrate a disaster in the kitchen
truck, turn up the oven, scorch the quail.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.680
It's like I'm watching my own execution.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.880
Perhaps influenced by Love's dying words...

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:54.479
We're perfect for each other.

00:06:54.479 --> 00:06:56.650
But bad..
for Henry.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:07:01.630
..Joe realises he might not be a good father
and if he stays he'll be locked up as her

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:05.110
accomplice, setting his son off on the same
damaging path as himself.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:08.740
So, he tearfully leaves his baby with Dante
and Lansing.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:14.031
And Henry's in safe, caring hands instead
of Dottie's unstable, sozzled ones or the

00:07:14.031 --> 00:07:17.129
lonely, potentially bullying hands of a group
home.

00:07:17.129 --> 00:07:23.540
So, hopefully for Henry, Joe's broken the
harmful cycle set in motion by his own parents.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:28.710
At the start of the finale, Love told Kiki
&amp; co they were a "bunch of scandal-hungry

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:29.710
crows"..

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:32.330
No amount of feasting on other people's sorrows
is gonna make your lives less hollow.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:37.159
But by the end of the episode, those same
people are having a really good go at proving

00:07:37.159 --> 00:07:42.770
Love wrong as they dine out on her misery,
building businesses profiting off her death.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:47.919
From the jokey pseudo-feminist rebrand of
her bakery targeted more at selling Insta-worthy

00:07:47.919 --> 00:07:53.430
t-shirts than good quality food like Love's;
Yelp suggests the scones are just okay.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:57.819
to the at-home test for poison inspired by
her use of toxic wolfsbane;

00:07:57.819 --> 00:08:01.200
to a self-help bestseller about kidnapping
and caging.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:04.430
Caged: A Radical Couple's Therapy Technique.

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:09.240
As for Marienne, she takes Love's advice to
get away from Joe, leaving no phone number

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:10.240
or address behind.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:14.289
Due to her ex-husband, she already knew the
dangers of toxic relationships.

00:08:14.289 --> 00:08:18.729
I promised myself, my next relationship would
be aboveboard and honest.

00:08:18.729 --> 00:08:22.310
And, though she'd pushed it aside, she'd had
a bad feeling in her gut about Joe.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:23.580
Something in me knew that it was too good
to be true.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:31.129
In fact, her words in that moment echo Beck's
view of Joe in the Season 1 finale:

00:08:31.129 --> 00:08:33.280
And you knew, somewhere deep, it was too good
to be true.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.099
Unlike Joe, who believes in fairy tales..

00:08:35.099 --> 00:08:39.510
How do I make you see I could be your happily
ever after?

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:42.280
..Marienne doesn't believe in damsels in distress.

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:45.690
Instead, her favourite fairy tale is Jack
And The Beanstalk.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.149
Jack was a little badass.

00:08:47.149 --> 00:08:49.120
I wanted to be him.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:50.120
Screw princesses.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:54.260
So, given all that then, when Joe wonders:
Did you pity me when you read what happened?

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:55.700
Did it erase the fear she planted?

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:56.980
Do you still think about us?

00:08:56.980 --> 00:09:00.790
I imagine Marienne's answer would be a big
fat "no"!

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:05.490
The season ends with Joe taking his creepy
stalking act on the international road..

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:09.630
I have to believe our paths are destined to
cross again.

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:14.640
Paris is his destination of choice as Marienne's
originally from there and she told him during

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:18.640
her custody battle that's where she'd run
to with her daughter if she thought her ex-husband

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:19.790
wouldn't find them.

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:22.630
And spend our days drawing outside Sacré-Coeur.

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:32.940
Though Marienne mentions the famous basilica
of Sacré-Coeur, he's actually here as it

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:38.209
has fantastic views of the Eiffel Tower, which
immediately signals to viewers where Joe is.

00:09:38.209 --> 00:09:43.580
The name of the café is "Le chasseur solitaire",
which translates into English as "The Lone

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:48.190
Hunter", brilliantly fitting for Joe Goldberg
and his continued solo predator activities.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:50.600
I think I'm meant to be a lone wolf.

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:55.209
It does feel kind of ironic that after Joe
lied about his ex, Candace, leaving him and

00:09:55.209 --> 00:10:00.010
running off to Europe, that's what seemingly
has actually happened with Marienne.

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:03.790
This isn't the first time that Paris has popped
up on the show as a place to get away and

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.339
start fresh either.

00:10:05.339 --> 00:10:09.290
Peach wanted Beck to move there with her and
live at her parents' flat.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:11.840
Paris could be a new beginning for the both
of us.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:16.670
And, after caging Delilah in season 2, Joe
suggested the French capital to Love as a

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:20.430
place to wipe the slate clean:
What if we leave together?

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:21.430
Start over.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:22.430
You could finish cooking school in Paris.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:27.370
By the way, those jingling bells on the café
door are meant to make us think of Beck, Joe's

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:32.139
first main infatuation in the series, which
in many ways indicates he's right back where

00:10:32.139 --> 00:10:33.139
he started.

00:10:33.139 --> 00:10:37.950
Yes, he's in a new city, a new country even,
but he's still the same old Joe.

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:42.510
The barista may call him "Nick", a sign that
he's taken on a new identity for this next

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:45.420
chapter, but Joe already has form for this.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:48.959
In LA, he kidnapped Will Bettelheim and stole
his identity;

00:10:48.959 --> 00:10:54.100
though he did eventually free him and they
kept in contact, so maybe Will helped him

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:57.190
out with a fake passport to get out of the
US.

00:10:57.190 --> 00:11:02.910
And perhaps Joe picked the name Nick, subconsciously
thinking of Dr Nicky, the man he falsely framed

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:05.170
for the murder of Beck in New York.

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:10.130
Although Joe's delusional antics in You are
intriguing to watch, in real life to keep

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:15.020
our personal details away from creeps and
snoopers like him, we all need to improve

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.020
our online security.

